From 798fd9a09765107dfe012b5f5603f3618dc035db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:14:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: no fault address from an abort whose FAR is not valid

Follow-up to "every exception from user mode becomes a real signal",
from a review of it:
- An external abort that the ISS marks FnV has no valid FAR. SIGBUS now
  carries address 0 instead of whatever FAR held. The syslog line still
  prints the ESR, so FnV is visible there.
- The comment on EXCP_ILL_STATE said an illegal exception return sets
  PSTATE.IL. An illegal return does not change the exception level, so
  PSTATE.IL at EL0 comes from a legal return whose SPSR had IL set.

trap_check (HaikuArmQemu private_workspace/trap-test.sh) still passes
14/14 under QEMU+HVF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
index dcf7c4aad4..58002391c1 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int.cpp
@@ -298,8 +298,8 @@ do_sync_handler(iframe * frame)
 	bool isExec = false;
 	switch (ESR_ELx_EXCEPTION(frame->esr)) {
 		case EXCP_ILL_STATE:
-			// PSTATE.IL, set by an illegal exception return. Clear it, or
-			// the signal handler could not run either.
+			// PSTATE.IL: the exception return into this thread had SPSR.IL
+			// set. Clear it, or the signal handler could not run either.
 			frame->spsr &= ~PSR_IL;
 			// fall through
 		case EXCP_UNKNOWN:
@@ -403,7 +403,8 @@ do_sync_handler(iframe * frame)
 					signalCode = BUS_ADRERR;
 				}
 				signalNumber = SIGBUS;
-				signalAddress = frame->far;
+				// FAR is not valid when the ISS says FnV (external aborts)
+				signalAddress = (frame->esr & ISS_DATA_FnV) != 0 ? 0 : frame->far;
 				break;
 			}
 
